Theory

Bubble Sort is a simple sorting algorithm used to arrange elements in ascending or descending order. It repeatedly compares two adjacent elements and swaps them if they are in the wrong order.

In each pass, the largest element moves to the end of the unsorted part of the array. This process continues until the whole array is sorted.

Algorithm
Start with the given array.
Compare two adjacent elements.
If the first element is greater than the second element, swap them.
Continue comparing adjacent elements up to the end of the array.
After one pass, the largest element reaches the last position.
Repeat the same process for the remaining unsorted elements.
Continue until no more elements need to be swapped.
Display the sorted array.
Stop.